WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:11.509
What up G? Welcome back to Thug
Notes. This week we keepin it Victorian with

00:00:11.509 --> 00:00:13.690
Great Expectations by Charles Dickens

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.539
This book tells the story of Pip, a
street kid who be shackin with his crooked

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:25.469
sister and her hubby Joe. One day while payin
his respects at his parents’ grave, a cracked

00:00:25.469 --> 00:00:30.879
out convict rolls up to him and demands some
food and a nail file to escape his chains.

00:00:30.879 --> 00:00:34.660
Pip helps a brotha out, but later sees that
fool get got by the po-lice.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.270
Later, an uppity cracker named
Pumblechook arranges for Pip to kick it with

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.780
a rich broad named Miss Haversham and her
adopted daughter Estella. Now Estella may

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.980
be fine, but she be actin a straight cock-tease
to my boy Pip. Pip be thinkin that Miss Haversham

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.350
wanna prime him to get paid like a gentleman,
but she shuts his ass down and tells him to

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:57.480
hustle as a blacksmith with his po Uncle Joe.
Then one day some lawyer named

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:04.019
Jaggers tells Pip that he bout to get PAID
and inherit a swoel fortune. So Pip kicks

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:08.600
Joe’s po ass to the curb and heads to London
where he gonna learn to be a playa. Pip be

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:13.020
thinkin that Miss Haversham gave him all dat
cash, so maybe she be preppin him to marry

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.889
Estella.

00:01:13.889 --> 00:01:18.100
One night Pip be visited by some
playa named Abel Magwitch, who turns out to

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.899
be dat convict from the graveyard. He tells
Pip that it was him who gave Pip all dem stacks

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:23.679
of cash.

00:01:23.679 --> 00:01:27.270
Now Pip be wiggin out that he ain’t bein
primed to marry Estella, so he

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.950
rolls up to that ho Haversham’s crib and
confesses his love for Estella. But that hood

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.200
rat shuts this stunna down.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.649
Years later, Pip dun fu**ed up and
ends up boned out. Uncle Joe does Pip one

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.340
last solid and pays off all his debt. Now
Pip be feelin like a fool for dissin him all

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.849
them years ago. So Pip decide to stop frontin
wit dem rich folk and keeps it real with the

00:01:47.849 --> 00:01:53.479
boy who got his back. Then one day while peepin
the old Haversham crib, Pip runs in to Estella

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:58.579
who be off the short lease of her ex-husband
and Haversham, and decide she wanna be cool

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:03.329
with Pip. At the end of the book, Pip say
he “saw no shadow of another parting from

00:02:03.329 --> 00:02:04.069
her.”

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.560
Now one of the main things my boy Charlie
D tryin to say up in here

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.470
is if you makin big ass assumptions about
what the future holds, you sho as hell got

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:19.250
anotha thing coming homeboy. You can see this
here disconnect between expectations and reality

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:23.860
in the character of Haversham. This broad
always wearin an old crusty wedding dress

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.780
even though she ain’t married. It’s like
she walkin around erry day showin that she

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.740
was expectin way more out of life than she
actually got.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:35.700
Likewise, Pip always expectin
righteous things to happen like Miss H makin

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.310
him a gentleman and gettin freaky with that
girl Estella. But this stunna is blind to

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.430
the peeps that actually got his back.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.170
For example, when Pip finds out it
was Abel that give him those stacks of cash

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:51.450
and not that hag Haversham, he gets all crunk
cuz it ain’t what he expected. When on the

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:54.900
real, he should be geeked up that he got himself
a sugar daddy.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.250
Another theme up in here is that havin mad
money corrupts yo mind

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:03.670
and yo social relations. Before Pip becomes
a rich play boy, that gitty cat Pumblechook

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.650
be disrespectin him all the time. But after
Pip makes bank, Pumblechook starts treatin

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.020
him like he da man.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:15.200
Also, when my boy Pip gets dem fat
pockets, he starts dissin Joe cuz he all po.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.640
On page 197, Pip says He would even PAY to
get Joe’s weak ass outta his face in spite

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:27.370
of the fact that on page 127, Pip straght
up calls this stunna an angel. Mo money, Mo

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.710
problems blood.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.950
Consider this sh** right here-
conflicting values in this playa’s life

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:37.240
be told trough the images of stars and fire.
That trick Estella’s name comes from a Latin

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:43.250
word that means star, whereas my man Joe be
associated with da forge and fireplace. Mah

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.350
honkie Dickens links that hoe with stars cuz
although stars may be pretty, they straight

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:51.930
up unreachable- just like Pip’s romantic
expectations. But on the other hand, fire

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:57.460
is of the earth, and Dickens links Joe with
fire to emphasize that down-home feeling of

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.750
a life in the hood without whack ass delusions.

